```css
.parent {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
}
```  

Or, use CSS Grid:  
```css
.parent {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
}
```  

Flexbox is the most reliable and modern approach.

Use `margin: 0 auto;` on the div, but only if it has a defined width. Without a width, auto margins won’t work. Example:

```css
.centered-div {
  width: 50%;
  margin: 0 auto;
}
```

Alternatively, use `flexbox` on the parent:

```css
.parent {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
}
```

Or `grid`:

```css
.parent {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
}
```
